_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 39
---
order: 39
---
short_label: I.39
---
statement: Equal triangles which are on the same base and on the same side are also in the same parallels.
---
proof:

<div class="just"><a href="../../postulates/post1/">I.Post.1</a></div>

Let *ABC* and *DBC* be equal triangles which are on the same base *BC* and on the same side of it. Join *AD.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="260" height="210" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="I.39 diagram" src="propI39.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "I.39",
        elements: [
            "B;point;free;40,170",
            "C;point;free;220,170",
            "A;point;free;80,40",
            "ABC;polygon;triangle;A,B,C",
            "AD';line;parallel;A,B,C;0;0;0",
            "D;point;lineSlider;AD',210,40",
            "BCD;polygon;triangle;B,C,D",
            "AD;line;connect;A,D",
            "E;point;lineSlider;B,D,165,40",
            "AE;line;connect;A,E",
            "CE;line;connect;C,E"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

I say that *AD* is parallel to *BC.*

<div class="just"><a href="../propI31/">I.31</a>, <a href="../../postulates/post1/">I.Post.1</a></div>

If not, draw *AE* through the point *A* parallel to the straight line *BC,* and join *EC.*

<div class="just"><a href="../propI37/">I.37</a></div>

Therefore the triangle *ABC* equals the triangle *EBC,* for it is on the same base *BC* with it and in the same parallels.

<div class="just"><a href="../../commonnotions/cn1/">C.N.1</a></div>

But *ABC* equals *DBC,* therefore *DBC* also equals *EBC,* the greater equals the less, which is impossible.

Therefore *AE* is not parallel to *BC.*

Similarly we can prove that neither is any other straight line except *AD,* therefore *AD* is parallel to *BC.*

Therefore *equal triangles which are on the same base and on the same side are also in the same parallels.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
<br clear="all">
---
body:

This is a partial converse to proposition [I.37](../propI37/), only partial since the two triangles *ABC* and *DBC* have to be on the same side of the line *BC.* If they weren't, then of course *AD* would not be parallel to *BC* but instead cross it at the midpoint

#### Use of Proposition 39

This proposition is used in [VI.2](/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI2/).
